    "created_at": "2015-09-28T15:32:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-09-28T15:32:52Z",
    "body": "> This adds callers.\n\nThose aren't needed for web compat either, I believe; I thought there was an existing issue about removing legacycaller from `HTMLFormControlsCollection`.\n\n> It also seems to be about explaining\n\nThe main difference between `HTMLCollection` and `HTMLFormControlsCollection` here is whether you have to do the `RadioNodeList` thing or whether you can just have a `getter Element (DOMString name)`, yes?  Again, the `RadioNodeList` thing here is not needed for web compat, unlike on `<form>`.\n\n> Presumably IE does have getters on `<form>`?\n\nYou mean `form.elements` is an `HTMLFormControlsCollection` in IE?  Yes, it is.  That part is true in all browsers in practice, though some of them claim it's an `HTMLCollection`... but return those `RadioNodeList` things anyway.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
