    "updated_at": "2015-09-28T17:30:56Z",
    "body": "1. I cannot find the issue to remove legacycaller from `HTMLFormControlsCollection`, but happy to make a PR to remove it and also from `HTMLOptionsCollection`. As I understand it from you `<embed>` and `<object>` might be harder. We could track those separately or just wait for browsers to move first.\n2. If `RadioNodeList` is only needed on `<form>` it seems like we should remove `HTMLFormControlsCollection` altogether since there would be nothing that expose it directly.\n3. Your last paragraph is confusing. I thought you said only `<form>` needs to support `RadioNodeList` and `<form>.elements` could become an \"ordinary\" `HTMLCollection`?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
