    "created_at": "2015-10-08T19:17:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-10-08T19:17:20Z",
    "body": "In that case I'm not sure I understand the difference in complexity. It sounds like the `HTMLFormControlsCollection` implementation in Gecko is tied to `HTMLFormElement` in a way that makes it non-trivial to quickly reuse it with `HTMLFieldSetElement`?\n\nIn Blink it looks like `HTMLFormControlsCollection` (wonderfully documented as \"just a big hack\") differs from `HTMLCollection` in more ways than the override in the IDL, so I'm not sure how to be confident that such a change wouldn't break much stuff.\n\nGiven that IE doesn't implement this at all, is removing it an option everyone would be open too if usage is low enough? That almost seems like less work than working through the details of this.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
