    "created_at": "2015-10-08T19:38:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-10-08T19:38:58Z",
    "body": "> In that case I'm not sure I understand the difference in complexity\n\nThe difference is that to implement `HTMLFormControlsCollection` properly you have to have additional notifications to add/remove things to the `RadioNodeLists` and convert from `RadioNodeList` to single nodes, etc.  On the other hand, an `HTMLCollection` with a filter is something that appears all over the DOM anyway and so doesn't need any new special notifications.\n\nAnd yes, form controls notify their form when they get added to it or removed from it, and it does the fairly nontrivial maintenance work for the `HTMLFormControlsCollection`.  As I said we _could_ make that work with fieldsets, at the cost of some bloat (controls have to keep track of their fieldset) and some performance (extra work on all the additions/removals to fieldset.  The question is whether that bloat and performance cost is worth it.\n\nWhat are the other differences between `HTMLFormControlsCollection` and `HTMLCollection` in Blink?\n\n> is removing it an option everyone would be open to\n\nI would be open to it, yes.  Though it does seem like there are decent use cases for walking the list of controls inside a fieldset in a sane way.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
