    "created_at": "2015-10-09T08:48:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-10-09T08:48:31Z",
    "body": "> What are the other differences between `HTMLFormControlsCollection` and `HTMLCollection` in Blink?\n\nSo there's a bunch of code, but on closer inspection it looks like it's all really for keeping track of what the associated elements are, with some caching, and then the `namedItem()` method, named getter and named property enumerator.\n\nAt the end of the day it doesn't look like the actual code to find the associated elements is shared for `form` and `fieldset`, however. Without attempting the change I dare not guess if using `HTMLCollection` instead would be a simplificiation or a complication, so I don't know what to suggest.\n\n@int32t, assuming you are tkent@chromium.org, you've poked a little bit at `HTMLFormControlsCollection`, do you have any thoughts on whether turning it into a `HTMLCollection` would be an improvement?\n",
